the premise of our book influencing up  is that in today's complex fast changing  world to really be successful it's no  longer sufficient just to do your job  one has to take initiative in seizing  new opportunities see new possibilities  new audiences new customers and solving  problems before they really develop this  also demands that one be able to  influence certainly your boss but also  those further up the organization and  the question is how do you influence  those that you can't control central to  the notion of influence is a law of  reciprocity and the law of reciprocity  says that if I do something for you you  owe me what then we expect to get paid  back for things that we do for other  people the phrase and honest day's work  for an honest day's pay symbolizes that  sort of exchange so what you want to do  to influence people that you don't have  formal authority over is to figure out  what they need and we use the concept of  currencies and think of multiple  currencies what does the other person  need do they need information do they  need support do they need going to a  third party and getting their sort of  agreement do they need to make sure you  stay within budget well what are their  major needs and what it is that you need  it may be very different than what the  other person needs and to influence  other people you need to give other  people what they need in exchange for  what you need  if you want to build a relationship with  your boss its first of all important to  do things which are trustworthy and  often withholding information breaks  trust often we raise an issue in a very  circuitous or indirect way and that  makes the boss suspicious the other  thing is to really be on the boss's side  you have to understand the boss's world  and we tend to see the world through our  eyes and not take the time of trying to  understand how the world seems through  the boss's eyes the main takeaway of the  book is that you an employee can be much  more powerful than you think you can be  and secondly that to be more powerful is  not to take away the power of others but  to build your own power and you can  build your own power in a win-win  situation power is not a fixed amount so  the more you have unless I have in most  cases of power is a variable it's  possible for you boss to be highly  powerful and for me to be powerful and  what we have seen too often is not that  the boss takes away the junior partners  power but the junior partner takes away  his or her own power and we want to give  it back
 

